WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.569
Apple’s new 2nd generation AirPods are finally
here, but to be completely honest, they’re

00:00:04.569 --> 00:00:08.380
a little bit underwhelming, at least compared
to all the leaks and rumors we’ve seen in

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:09.380
recent months.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:14.120
There’s no active noise cancellation, no
health monitoring features, and worst of all,

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.530
they still only come in white.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:20.240
But to be fair, Samsung’s new Galaxy Buds
also don’t get any of that apart from the

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.290
color options.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:25.480
So if you’re trying to choose between both,
it’s really gonna come down to connectivity,

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.980
sound quality, and of course, price.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.869
So before I get to who should upgrade to the
new AirPods and who shouldn’t, let’s quickly

00:00:31.869 --> 00:00:33.590
run through all of the changes.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:38.180
First up, of course, is the new Wireless charging
case, which is completely optional and will

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.480
work using any regular Qi charger.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.680
The charging speed is still unknown but the
battery is comparatively small so it shouldn’t

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:45.910
take very long.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:50.120
Next up, the AirPods finally have Hey Siri
support, so it’s much more convenient to

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.360
make calls, change the volume, or anything
else.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.960
The way it works is by using a new accelerometer
which detects the motion of your jawbone when

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.220
you say the words “Hey Siri.”

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:05.040
Now here’s the big change, the new AirPods
pack Apple’s new H1 headphone chip, which

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.870
provides a faster and more stable wireless
connection to your devices.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:13.870
Now the W1 chip in the original AirPods was
revolutionary, it seriously blew Bluetooth

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:17.470
out of the water with its quick connection
speed and battery life management.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:22.130
The H1 chip boasts lowered latency, faster
connection time for phone calls and it can

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:25.300
switch between active devices up to 2x faster.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:29.140
The only problem I have with my original AirPods
is that they take a while to connect to my

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:33.780
Mac, but thankfully, the $3 app called ToothFairy
fixed that issue.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.640
So if the new H1 chip can solve these connection
issues, that’s gonna be a game-changer.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.390
The new AirPods get an extra hour of battery
life during phone calls, up to 3 hours instead

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.110
of 2, but listening time stays the same.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:50.460
An update we’re happy to see is the switch
to Bluetooth 5, so it now matches the X-line

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:54.920
of iPhones and the Apple Watch Series 4, so
you get increased range, which is huge for

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.380
those who like to set their phone down and
move around.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:00.490
So with that out of the way, let’s get to
who should upgrade.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:03.840
First of all, if your current AirPods are
in good condition and work great for your

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.920
needs, I honestly wouldn’t upgrade.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.320
And if you’re thinking of just grabbing
the wireless charging case, I personally don’t

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.390
think it’s worth it.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:14.140
The wired charging speed is just too dang
quick.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:18.200
We’re talking 15 minutes of charging for
3 hours of listening time.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.760
I only use my AirPods when I need them for
work, so I literally only plug them in every

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:23.760
2 weeks.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:27.750
The times when I do use them more often, I
only plug it in once a week, so wireless charging

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.510
would be a huge waste for me.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:33.920
Now if you’re the type that listens to music
literally every day, all day, and you love

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.610
using wireless charging, it makes sense.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:40.370
Otherwise, simply plugging them in every evening
for half an hour will do the job.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:44.990
The interesting thing is that the wireless
charging case only costs an extra $40 if you

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:50.090
buy the new AirPods instead of $80 alone,
so I would honestly just upgrade to AirPods

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:52.340
2 instead of just buying the case by itself.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:56.540
Now if you’ve never owned AirPods, now’s
the time, because they have some pretty great

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:59.930
upgrades and they’re the same price as the
original AirPods were.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.090
Trust me, you’re gonna love AirPods, so
order them now before they sell out.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:07.960
If you own an Apple Watch, AirPods are gonna
be your best friend, since you can easily

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:13.090
adjust the volume with the crown and instantly
take phone calls from your watch, so I recommend

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:14.959
them for any Apple Watch owner.

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:19.400
Now the biggest question many of you are gonna
have is if the sound quality has significantly

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:24.400
improved, and unfortunately, Apple’s website
doesn’t mention any major sound quality

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.920
improvements, so we won’t know for sure
until we try them out.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.840
We ordered a pair of AirPods 2 this morning
and the first thing we’ll do is compare

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:33.640
the sound quality to the original AirPods
and Samsung’s new Galaxy Buds, so if you’re

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:37.550
not already subscribed, click that button
to sub now so you don’t miss out on those

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.550
videos!

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.470
This has been Vadim with Max Tech, thanks
for watching, and we’ll see you in the next

